		(uuid "05cf996e-008f-4a8d-990e-bc11862e612d")
	)
	(text_box "CAUTION: ISOLATION SPACING (FSAE 2027 EV.8.3.2, EV.7.5.7)\n\n1. EV.8.3.2: the BMS must have galvanic isolation at every Module-to-Module boundary. U2/U3 provide it. All slaves are identical, so every barrier is designed for the worst case: full pack voltage, <128S x 4.2 V = 537.6 V> max (EV.3.3.2 limit: 600 V DC).\n2. EV.7.5.7 spacing, 300-600 V DC row:\nClearance (through air): 3.0 mm\nCreepage, general (uncoated): 20.0 mm\nCreepage, under conformal coating: 4.0 mm\n3. This board IS conformally coated, so the 4.0 mm creepage and 3.0 mm clearance apply. Uncoated it would NOT comply (7.11 mm < 20 mm).\n4. Rule applies on the same layer AND between layers. Keep >= 4.0 mm on every layer between chip-side copper (inner GND pours, vias, TVS / CT-cap pads) and cable-side copper (U2/U3 pins 4-6, J1/J2). Actual: 7.11 mm transformer pad gap (SM91502ALA land pattern).\n5. No plated holes, vias or copper pours inside the isolation zone.\n6. Mark the zone on top AND bottom silkscreen (boundary lines + \"ISOLATION ZONE\"), per EV.7.5.6 / EV.7.5.7a.\n7. U2/U3 isolation rating and the daisy-chain cable insulation must be rated >= max TS voltage (EV.5.2.1, EV.7.3.2).\n8. Keep a spare coated board or photos for inspection (EV.7.5.8)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 137.16 172.72 0)
		(size 106.68 40.64)
		(margins 2 2 2 2)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 250 236 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "20e24bfa-a15e-4c6a-9cec-a7ab7d02680e")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE: DAISY CHAIN ISOLATION\n\n1. Transformer isolation per SLUSE81F Table 8-5 / Fig 8-9: R_TERM 1 kΩ, R_SERIES 49.9 Ω, C_BYPASS 220 pF/50 V C0G, centre-tap cap 100 pF to GND, TVS PESD1CAN on chip side.\n2. Cable-side centre taps (U2-5, U3-5) are left NC per Fig 8-9.\n3. Stack device: RX tied to CVDD, TX and NFAULT left NC (SLUSE81F 8.2.1.2.6).\n4. U3 is drawn with chip-side pins 1/3 opposite to U2. Polarity is preserved end to end (P->P, N->N).\n5. Ring architecture: COMH (J2) goes up the stack, COML (J1) goes down. J1 = 43650-0200 single-row, J2 = 43045-0200 dual-row so a cable cannot connect COMH to COMH.\n6. Use the same transformer PN on both ends of every link, including the master (TI SLVAEP4 5.1)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 55.88 132.08 0)
		(size 76.2 35.56)
		(margins 2 2 2 2)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d3a53d42-2353-40fb-ba88-dd0ac93b5dd8")
	)
	(text_box "LAYOUT NOTE: DAISY CHAIN (TI SLUSE81F 10.1.4, Fig 10-3)\n\n1. COMH and COML pairs: short, straight, same layer, parallel, length matched. No vias in the pairs.\n2. R_TERM and C_BYPASS close to U1 pins 40-43.\n3. Solid GND under the chip-side parts (R, C, TVS) is required for the bypass and TVS returns. Keep unrelated traces out of this area, and never route a COM pair across a plane seam.\n4. No copper on ANY layer under the transformer bodies or between the transformer cable side and J1/J2.\n5. Transformer barrier: 7.11 mm pad gap meets EV.7.5.7 300-600 V coated creepage (4.0 mm) and clearance (3.0 mm). Keep >= 4.0 mm on all layers. No plated holes, vias or pours inside the isolation zone.\n6. Place each transformer next to its connector.\n7. TP11-TP14: bare SMD pads on the trace, no stubs."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 55.88 172.72 0)
		(size 76.2 38.1)
		(margins 2.25 2.25 2.25 2.25)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 0 0 255 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 0 255 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fd8b5fa4-a69f-4a56-a29c-8922715198aa")
	)
